cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "dualmesh-multiphysics: coupled heat transfer, solid mechanics and incompressible flow by the finite element method and the dual mesh control domain method"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 0.2.0
license: LGPL-2.1-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/MohamedAbdulHameed/dualmesh-multiphysics"
url: "https://github.com/MohamedAbdulHameed/dualmesh-multiphysics"
abstract: >-
  dualmesh-multiphysics solves coupled problems of heat transfer, solid
  mechanics and incompressible flow, and partial differential equations
  written as text. It discretizes a problem by the finite element method
  (FEM), and a problem with a flow by the dual mesh control domain method
  (DMCDM), which conserves the transported quantity in every control domain. Coupled
  problems are solved together by Newton's method, with exact Jacobians from
  automatic differentiation. The core is written in C++17 with PETSc and MPI,
  and it is driven from Python or from YAML case files.
keywords:
  - dual mesh control domain method
  - finite element method
  - fluid dynamics
  - solid mechanics
  - heat transfer
  - partial differential equations
  - multiphysics
authors:
